        "# FLUX.2 Klein Base 9B: image + text editing\n\n1. Choose the previous completed image in Reference image.\n2. Put 'Required change: ...' and 'Result to show: ...' at the top of Edit instruction / target state. Keep the general no-text instructions underneath.\n3. Queue the workflow. Use each new result as the reference for the next step.\n\nSettings: Euler, 20 steps, CFG 7, about 1 megapixel. The seed control randomizes between queued edits. The Python app also gives every editing call a fresh random seed; its first text-only image uses seed 42.\n\nAll images must be text-free, including packaging and interfaces. Edits remove existing writing from the reference. Keep written procedure details outside the images.\n\nThis canvas mirrors workflow_edit_api.json, including models, prompts, sampling, and image-reference connections. The app uses workflow_api.json for image one and workflow_edit_api.json for later images. Update the API file too if you change this canvas manually.\n\nAll nodes are built into current ComfyUI. Model files and setup instructions are listed in README.md."
      ]
    }
